### ==========================================
### 1. Exercise CRUD
### ==========================================

### 1.1 Create a CHOICE exercise
POST http://localhost:3000/exercise HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "description": "กรุณาเลือกคำตอบที่ถูกต้อง",
    "skillId": 1,
    "skillLevel": 1,
    "expectTime": 60,
    "type": "CHOICE",
    "choices": [
        { "script": "ตัวเลือกที่ 1", "isAnswer": true },
        { "script": "ตัวเลือกที่ 2", "isAnswer": false },
        { "script": "ตัวเลือกที่ 3", "isAnswer": false },
        { "script": "ตัวเลือกที่ 4", "isAnswer": false }
    ]
}

### 1.2 Create a FILL_IN_BLANK exercise
POST http://localhost:3000/exercise HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "description": "คำสั่งสำหรับวนลูปคือคำสั่งใด?",
    "skillId": 1,
    "skillLevel": 2,
    "expectTime": 45,
    "type": "FILL_IN_BLANK",
    "fillInBlank": "for",
    "isCasesensitive": "NO"
}

### 1.3 Update an exercise (edit description/skill/level and choices)
PUT http://localhost:3000/exercise/1 HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "description": "กรุณาเลือกคำตอบที่ถูกต้อง (แก้ไข)",
    "skillLevel": 2,
    "choices": [
        { "script": "ตัวเลือกที่ 1 (แก้ไข)", "isAnswer": false },
        { "script": "ตัวเลือกที่ 2 (แก้ไข)", "isAnswer": true }
    ]
}

### 1.4 Get one exercise
GET http://localhost:3000/exercise/1 HTTP/1.1

### 1.5 List exercises
GET http://localhost:3000/exercise HTTP/1.1

### 1.6 Delete (soft-delete -> status inactive)
DELETE http://localhost:3000/exercise/1 HTTP/1.1

### ==========================================
### 2. KT-IDEM Flow via NestJS Gateway (:3000)
### Flow: Client -> NestJS (:3000) -> FastAPI (:8000)
### ==========================================

### 2.1 Register Skill via NestJS
POST http://localhost:3000/kt/skill HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "skillId": "control_flow",
  "pL0": 0.3,
  "pT": 0.2
}

### 2.2 Register Item via NestJS
POST http://localhost:3000/kt/item HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "itemId": "cf-for-01",
  "skillId": "control_flow",
  "pG": 0.25,
  "pS": 0.1,
  "difficultyLabel": 2
}

### 2.3 Submit Attempt via NestJS (Student answers correctly)
POST http://localhost:3000/kt/attempt HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "studentId": "std_001",
  "itemId": "cf-for-01",
  "correct": true
}

### 2.4 Submit 2nd Attempt via NestJS (Student answers incorrectly)
POST http://localhost:3000/kt/attempt HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "studentId": "std_001",
  "itemId": "cf-for-01",
  "correct": false
}

### 2.5 Get Student Mastery via NestJS
GET http://localhost:3000/kt/mastery/std_001/control_flow HTTP/1.1


### ==========================================
### 3. Direct FastAPI Endpoints (:8000)
### For directly testing python microservice
### ==========================================

### 3.1 Health Check
GET http://localhost:8000/health HTTP/1.1

### 3.2 Register Skill Directly (snake_case)
POST http://localhost:8000/kt/skill HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "skill_id": "math_algebra",
  "p_l0": 0.2,
  "p_t": 0.15
}

### 3.3 Register Item Directly (snake_case)
POST http://localhost:8000/kt/item HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "item_id": "alg-01",
  "skill_id": "math_algebra",
  "p_g": 0.2,
  "p_s": 0.15,
  "difficulty_label": 1
}

### 3.4 Submit Attempt Directly (snake_case)
POST http://localhost:8000/kt/attempt HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "student_id": "std_002",
  "item_id": "alg-01",
  "correct": true
}

### 3.5 Get Student Mastery Directly
GET http://localhost:8000/kt/mastery/std_002/math_algebra HTTP/1.1



